title: Dynamics
manual: structure/#c2-forcefields

Run an interactive molecular dynamics simulation or a geometry relaxation on a system
using a built-in force field, and watch it in the view. While a run is active, the
"Interact (MD)" view mode lets you steer it with the mouse: drag an atom, or translate or
rotate a whole molecule. The simulation parameters are kept on the system and shared with
the Builder relaxation and the Rattle Structure window.

# Options
- Method: the force field for energies, forces and stress (UFF, DREIDING, EAM, TIP4P
  water or, when the libraries are available, GFN1-xTB, GFN2-xTB and GFN-FF). Only the
  methods that apply to the system are listed.
- Potential (EAM): the embedded-atom potential file, from the catalog of potentials that
  cover the elements of the system.
- Dynamics (NVT): animate the system at constant temperature. Relaxation: move the atoms
  to the nearest energy minimum.
- Temperature (K): the thermostat temperature of the NVT run.
- Time step (au): the integration time step, in atomic units.
- RUN starts the simulation and Stop ends it; "Reset" restores the initial geometry and
  removes all motion.

# Results
Once a run has started, the "Status" section lists the current temperature, the EAM
potential in use, the potential energy in Hartree and kcal/mol and, for a relaxation,
the largest atomic force; for dynamics, the elapsed time in fs and, in crystals, the
pressure in GPa. Error messages and automatic stops are shown below the table. The atoms
move in the view as the simulation advances.

# Notes
- The geometry of the system changes during the run; use "Reset", or Restore in the
  Builder, to go back to the original structure.
- A relaxation moves only the atoms selected in the view, or all of them if there is no
  selection.
